{"timestamp": "2026-08-16T10:37:58.506367", "tool": "write_file", "args": {"content": "Johannes Gutenberg invented the movable-type printing press around 1440, revolutionizing book production by replacing slow, hand-copying methods. This technology, which used reusable metal type, allowed for the rapid mass production of texts. The printing press was instrumental in spreading literacy, standardizing languages, and facilitating the rapid exchange of ideas during the Renaissance and Reformation.", "filename": "demo_article_summary.txt"}, "status": "allowed", "reason": "ok", "previous_content": "Johannes Gutenberg invented the movable-type printing press around 1440, revolutionizing book production by replacing slow, hand-copying methods. This technology, which used reusable metal type, allowed for the rapid mass production of texts. The printing press was instrumental in spreading literacy, standardizing languages, and facilitating the rapid exchange of ideas during the Renaissance and Reformation."}
